<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Results and Discussion</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All <span id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">frontier-model</span> comparisons use <span id="S6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">n=100 (Q1–Q100)</span>
from the FACTS public split. <span id="S6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fine-tuned models</span> use
<span id="S6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">n=500 (Q1–Q500)</span> from the same public split. We use
<span id="S6.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">sequential selection</span> as ordered in the official notebook for
<span id="S6.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">reproducibility</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Exoskeleton Reasoning yields consistent improvements across all model
families, with large effect sizes (Cohen’s d &gt; 0.8).
Accuracy gains were <span id="S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">statistically significant (p &lt;
0.001)</span> and <span id="S6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">empirically stable across runs</span>.</p>
</div>
